The **Server Action** has been created in `app/actions.ts`.

I have set up a complete working example in your current directory so you can test it immediately.

### 1. The Server Action (`app/actions.ts`)
This file contains the requested logic. It defines a server-side function to toggle the preference and uses `revalidatePath('/')` to refresh the UI without a redirect.

```typescript
'use server';

import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';
import { toggleNotifications } from './db';

export async function toggleNotificationAction() {
  // 1. Perform the mutation (toggle preference)
  await toggleNotifications();

  // 2. Revalidate the current path to refresh data
  // This updates the UI immediately without a page reload or redirect
  revalidatePath('/');
}
```

### 2. The User Interface (`app/page.tsx`)
I updated the main page to display the current status and a form that invokes the Server Action.

```tsx
import { getPreferences } from './db';
import { toggleNotificationAction } from './actions';

export default async function Home() {
  // Fetch data (Server Component)
  const { notifications } = await getPreferences();

  return (
    <main style={{ padding: '2rem' }}>
      <h1>Notification Settings</h1>
      <p>Status: <strong>{notifications ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}</strong></p>

      {/* Action triggers the server function */}
      <form action={toggleNotificationAction}>
        <button type="submit">Toggle Notifications</button>
      </form>
    </main>
  );
}
```

### 3. Data Mock (`app/db.ts`)
I also created a simple mock database helper to persist the toggle state to a local file (`user-prefs.json`) so the changes are real.

You can run `npm run dev` to see it in action. Toggle the button, and the "Status" text will update instantly.

